  "details": "\r\n<p>The estate was confirmed as possession of the bishoprics of Cologne and Metz by king Sigebert III in 640/647. In the charter <em>Tribonum</em> is said to have belonged to queen Brunhilda (d. 613) and later king Clotaire II (d. 614) and Dagobert I (d. 639).</p>\r\n",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An estate formely belonging to Queen Brunhilda, daugther of the Visigoth king Athanagild and married to king Sigebert I",
